ROOT (NE) OPERATIONS LOG — SEALED
CLASSIFICATION: RESTRICTED — post-dissolution review copy

Root, the covert foundation-division formerly led by Danzo Shimura,
operated apart from the standing ANBU and reported to no one but its
commander. Following its formal dissolution, surviving operation logs
were sealed for review.

Recovered Log Themes (redacted):
- Long-term deep-cover placements, including operatives conditioned
  through the silencing seal to prevent disclosure of division secrets.
- Involvement in the internal handling of the Uchiha clan situation
  prior to the massacre (cross-reference restricted; see classified
  Uchiha report — access gated).
- Off-book intelligence operations conducted without Hokage sign-off.

Review Finding: Numerous actions were taken outside lawful authority.
No successor covert body is authorized. Files retained for the record
and for the Sixth Hokage's ANBU review. Do not action without the
Hokage's seal.
